# Testing Local Flow Plugins

Local plugins import via `FlowHelpers/*` path alias (resolved by `moduleNameMapper` in jest.config.js). This causes two gotchas:

## Mocking default exports (fileMoveOrCopy, etc.)

Use `__esModule: true` in the factory, then `require` the mock reference separately. Do NOT reference `const` variables in the factory (they're `undefined` due to hoisting).

```typescript
jest.mock('../../../../../../FlowPluginsTs/FlowHelpers/1.0.0/fileMoveOrCopy', () => ({
  __esModule: true,
  default: jest.fn().mockResolvedValue(true),
}));

const { default: mockFileMoveOrCopy } = require('../../../../../../FlowPluginsTs/FlowHelpers/1.0.0/fileMoveOrCopy');
```

## Mocking methods/lib

```typescript
jest.mock('../../../../../../methods/lib', () => () => ({
  loadDefaultValues: jest.fn((inputs) => inputs),
}));
```

## moduleNameMapper

`jest.config.js` maps `^FlowHelpers/(.*)$` → `<rootDir>/FlowPluginsTs/FlowHelpers/$1`. This was added to support local plugins; without it, any import from `FlowHelpers/*` fails in tests.
